          "A2": {
            "value": "",
            "readOnly": true
          },
          "A3": {
            "value": "(1) CCR Finding & Profit Quality:",
            "readOnly": true,
            "bold": true
          },
          "B3": {
            "value": "Cumulative 5-year CCR of 23% is deep red zone, well below FMCG threshold of 85%. Only ₹84 crore of the reported ₹362 crore PAT has converted to operating cash. FY16 CCR collapsed to 12%, signalling acute stress in underlying business operations and cash generation. Reported profit is NOT credible; likely absorbed by working capital management rather than genuine earnings.",
            "readOnly": true
          },
          "A4": {
            "value": "",
            "readOnly": true
          },
          "A5": {
            "value": "(2) Balance Sheet Absorption & Diagnosis:",
            "readOnly": true,
            "bold": true
          },
          "B5": {
            "value": "Receivables grew ₹245 crore (11x increase vs 3.4x revenue growth). Inventory grew ₹65 crore. Payables grew ₹30 crore. Net working capital absorption ≈ ₹280 crore, matching phantom profit within rounding. Receivables days extended from 42 (FY13) to 136 (FY17)—physically implausible for perishable beverage business with shelf-life constraints. Diagnosis: aggressive revenue recognition (possible channel stuffing) masking slowing underlying demand and cash conversion. Sales are being pushed into distribution channel without corresponding cash collection.",
            "readOnly": true
          },
          "A6": {
            "value": "",
            "readOnly": true
          },
          "A7": {
            "value": "(3) Rating & Rationale:",
            "readOnly": true,
            "bold": true
          },
          "B7": {
            "value": "SELL / Reduce with aggressive target price cut of 50–70%. Cumulative capex (₹708 cr) cannot be funded by cumulative CFO (₹84 cr)—gap of ₹624 cr bridged by debt growth (₹178 cr) and equity raises, indicating deteriorating financial flexibility and unsustainable capital structure. Combined with phantom profit and receivables anomalies, the business model is broken and equity at severe risk of impairment.",
            "readOnly": true
          }
        }
